WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.234
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:04.167
We're hanging out with
Miley Cyrus and Pete Davidson!

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:06.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:08.000
Two of the best out there.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.367
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:12.834
You two are hosting a live
New Year's Eve show on NBC.

00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:15.334
It's called
"Miley's New Year's Eve Party."

00:00:15.334 --> 00:00:17.801
Why did you decide to do
a New Year's Eve party?

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:21.834
-So, one thing I think that gets
focused on at New Year's time is

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:24.667
what's to come, being
optimistic, being hopeful

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:27.801
about all these things that
haven't happened yet,

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:29.834
that we have no proof
are going to happen.

00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:33.100
And we kind of erase everything
that did happen

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.801
and we forget to honor it
and look backwards too

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:39.100
and look at the -- even these
last, you know, year and a half,

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.667
two years has been rough,
but there's these

00:00:40.667 --> 00:00:44.067
micro moments of happiness
I'm sure all of us can find.

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:46.334
Mine was --
I'm recently an auntie.

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:48.133
So I have a little nephew now.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.968
-Yeah, that's great news.

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:52.067
-You know, even though this year
has been hard,

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:53.534
the last year and a half
has been hard,

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:56.234
you find those things that were
positive in the year before.

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:58.601
And you still are gonna look
forward to what hasn't happened

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:01.133
yet but I think just honoring
both sides of that.

00:01:01.133 --> 00:01:03.200
So I wanted to bring
that approach.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.601
And I also wanted to do
something that's obviously

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:07.734
traditional but I knew
that we would do it in a way

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.868
that is unique
and unconventional.

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:13.434
And we did that with
starting by going to Miami.

00:01:13.434 --> 00:01:15.367
-So you're doing it from Miami?

00:01:15.367 --> 00:01:16.434
-From Miami.

00:01:16.434 --> 00:01:17.701
-That's going to be a party.

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:19.133
-I don't like to be cold.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:20.367
That's why I'm in this.

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:22.167
I packed for your studio.
-Yes.

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:24.501
-And so that was
one of the things I thought

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:27.067
all these other shows, people
are going to have on big coats.

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:28.767
Everyone is going to be shaking
and freezing and then

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:30.400
I'm going to have no clothes on
per usual.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:31.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:32.901
He'll be funny
and I'll be naked,

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:33.968
and together, we got a show.

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:36.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh, my God.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.734
That's a promo right there.
-It's perfect.

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:40.834
-You've done Times Square before
on New Year's.

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.534
-Yes.
-I remember seeing you perform.

00:01:42.534 --> 00:01:45.667
-So I had -- Yeah, I was
a little scarred from that

00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:48.567
because this was in my day of
wearing the Hannah wig.

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:51.200
-Yeah.
-And it rained and then it was,

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.400
like, hailing and snowing,
and actually, you know,

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.100
like, when you've seen the --
like, a kid getting their tongue

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.534
stuck to the telephone pole
or something.

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:59.133
That happened but with my wig.

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:01.367
It got iced to my skin.

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:05.133
It got frozen to my head from it
being so cold outside.

00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:06.133
-How did you get it off?

00:02:06.133 --> 00:02:07.701
-I had to wait until it melted.

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:08.834
-Holy moly!

00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:11.100
-My mom just was like...
[ Heavy breathing ]

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:14.100
...on my head until I could get
the wig off.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.634
-Oh, my gosh.
-Yeah.

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.400
-Pete, how did you get
the [bleep] off your shoulder?

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:19.767
-I went...

00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:21.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:22.334
-That's interesting.

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:24.467
-That's not exactly
what happened.

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:28.334
-Miley, you're also overseeing
all the musical performances.

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:30.434
-Yes.
-Which I think you have,

00:02:30.434 --> 00:02:33.601
like Questlove, have
a encyclopedic brain

00:02:33.601 --> 00:02:35.033
when it comes to music.

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:37.367
-Yeah, we share
a lot of the same love

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:39.534
for the same artists too,
which is why I was so excited

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:41.701
to perform with the Roots,
but, yes, because I --

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:43.300
-You love music.
You know everything.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.534
-I was telling you that I
actually have my Spotify --

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:48.000
You know, they tell you what
you've been listening to

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.767
throughout the year
and who you listen to the most.

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:50.968
It said that I listen to

00:02:50.968 --> 00:02:54.467
97% more music
than the average user.

00:02:54.467 --> 00:02:55.767
-Human.
-Yeah.

00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:57.801
So I listen to a lot of music
all the time

00:02:57.801 --> 00:02:59.567
and I'm just constantly
discovering.

00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:03.234
But what's fun is to discover
something that's older

00:03:03.234 --> 00:03:07.200
that I can kind of reinvent
and introduce to my audience

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.601
who wouldn't know
some of these songs.

00:03:08.601 --> 00:03:11.033
So I'm -- That's one of the
things I'm most excited about is

00:03:11.033 --> 00:03:13.834
this show is -- yes, it's kind
of a variety show

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:16.767
because there will be so much
variety and artistry

00:03:16.767 --> 00:03:18.801
and I don't think one genre

00:03:18.801 --> 00:03:21.801
is better or more genuine
than another.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.367
I think that there's a space for
all of it

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:24.701
and I want to celebrate
and honor all of it.

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:26.100
-Mix it up.
-Yeah.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.868
-Pete, last time you were
on our show, you told me

00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:30.200
that you were taking
singing lessons.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.267
-Ha!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:33.701
-Are you still taking
the lessons?

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:35.100
-Yeah, yeah, kind of, yeah.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.367
-Yeah. And will you, maybe,
sing on New Year's Eve?

00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:40.567
-Absolutely not. No.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:43.100
-Even by midnight?
Closer to midnight? No?

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.334
-Maybe, maybe.

00:03:44.334 --> 00:03:45.868
-Alright, okay.
Alright, very good.

00:03:45.868 --> 00:03:47.634
Pete Davidson, Miley Cyrus.

